// Unacknowledged data is retransmitted after 300, 600 and 1200 ms gaps.
// The fixed socket RTO backs off once per expiry, capped at 60 seconds.
// The ACK at 2.2 s stops retransmission. New data arrives at 4.7 s, past
// the 4.5 s deadline that would have fired without that ACK.
// The 100-byte echo remains below one MSS and repeats the original segment.
// Cubic's RTO window is one effective MSS, 1460 bytes. The 100-byte
// retransmissions and later echo fit it without changing these packets.

0     < S 0:0(0) win 64240 <mss 1460,nop,nop,sackOK,nop,wscale 7>
+0    > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,wscale 2,sackOK,eol,eol,eol>
+0    < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 502
+0    < P. 1:101(100) ack 1 win 502
+0    > P. 1:101(100) ack 101 win 32768
+0.3  > P. 1:101(100) ack 101 win 32768
+0.6  > P. 1:101(100) ack 101 win 32768
+1.2  > P. 1:101(100) ack 101 win 32768
+0.1  < . 101:101(0) ack 101 win 502
+2.5  < P. 101:201(100) ack 101 win 502
+0    > P. 101:201(100) ack 201 win 32768
+0    < . 201:201(0) ack 201 win 502
+0    < F. 201:201(0) ack 201 win 502
+0    > . 201:201(0) ack 202 win 32768
+0    > F. 201:201(0) ack 202 win 32768
+0    < . 202:202(0) ack 202 win 502
